Third-party code and assets in this repository
----------------------------------------------

air-gestures (https://gitlab.com/896kb/air-gestures), Copyright (c) 2026 896kb, MIT License
(LICENSE-air-gestures): the band link this project grew from (band/, rust/).

kinesis (https://github.com/callbacked/kinesis), Copyright (c) 2026 callbacked, MIT License
(LICENSE-kinesis): the Meta Neural Band protocol, ported to Rust in rust/band-core/, and the
companion's Meta sign-in and band claim, ported to Kotlin in
phone/src/main/java/dev/lumen/companion/meta/ (MetaAuth, MetaPairClient, MetaLoginActivity;
the client ids, routes, request fields and callback check) with their tests; and the band's
handwriting (BandModelCapture.swift and ExperimentalHandwritingDecoder.swift), ported to Rust
in rust/band-core/src/model_capture.rs and handwriting.rs and modified to find the band's
settings by name; and the air cursor (AirCursor.swift, and BandModel.swift's cursor switch, clicks
and late-data handling), ported to Rust in rust/band-core/src/pointer.rs and
rust/bridge/src/controller.rs, with its pointer pacer ported to Kotlin in
phone/src/main/java/dev/lumen/companion/computer/PointerPacer.kt.

R08 Access Bridge (https://github.com/Anezium/R08-Access-Bridge), Copyright 2026 Anezium,
Apache License, Version 2.0 (LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt). The glasses' input, navigation,
settings screen and self-arm are derived from it and modified for the Meta Neural Band and
Lumen's grid, in app/src/main/java/dev/lumen/glasses/: AccessibilityNavigator,
AccessibilityWindowRoots, LauncherNavigator, GestureDispatcher, GlassesAction,
RokidSystemActions, BandAccessibilityService, MainActivity, BootReceiver, BridgeCommandActivity,
BridgeProtocol, PrivilegedShortcutBridge, LocalSelfArmStatus, SelfArmController,
SelfArmLocalAdbBootstrapper, SelfArmWirelessAdbController, SelfArmWirelessDebuggingAutomator,
SelfArmSettingsTextMatcher, and the ReadEra, ArBook and NewPipe compatibility modes
(ReaderaCompatibility, ArbookCompatibility, NewPipeCompatibility); and the helper scripts in
tools/. Each of these files says so in its header. R08 Access Bridge's NOTICE:

    R08 Access Bridge
    Copyright 2026 Anezium

    This product includes software developed by Anezium (https://github.com/Anezium).

    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Thanks to Anezium for R08 Access Bridge, and for licensing it for this project: it showed that
the Rokid glasses can be driven through an accessibility service and armed from the glasses
themselves, and most of what makes Lumen usable day to day comes from it.

Rokid Nexus (https://github.com/Anezium/Rokid-Nexus), Copyright Anezium, Apache License,
Version 2.0 (LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt). Ported and modified in
phone/src/main/java/dev/lumen/companion/relay/ (and their tests): NotificationTextExtractor,
SensitiveNotificationDetector and AndroidSensitiveNotificationDetector, from plugins/relay.
The notification filtering and the view-only inbox follow the Relay plugin's design. The
dictation engines in phone/src/main/java/dev/lumen/companion/speech/ follow
phone-hub/.../speech/ (the engines and their model ids, endpoints and message formats, the
transcription languages, the voice activity thresholds, the patience levels and the encrypted
key store), rewritten for this app's continuous dictation. The glasses' hand-off to the accessibility switch
during setup (app/src/main/java/dev/lumen/glasses/AccessibilityHandoff.kt) is derived from
glasses-hub's SelfArmAccessibilityHandoff.kt.

rokid-r08-wake (https://github.com/hacha/rokid-r08-wake), Copyright (c) 2026 hacha, MIT
License (LICENSE-rokid-r08-wake): the loopback self-arm technique that R08 Access Bridge's
accessibility watchdog recovery, and so Lumen's, is built on. A short part of SelfArmController
follows its SelfArm code.

Noto Sans (app/src/main/assets/fonts/ and phone/src/main/res/font/), Copyright 2022 The Noto
Project Authors, SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1 (app/src/main/assets/fonts/OFL.txt).

The glasses' screens follow the design tokens (colours, text styles, spacing, radii, focus
ramp and timing) of the Meta Ray-Ban Display UI Toolkit
(https://github.com/facebook/meta-ray-ban-display-ui-toolkit-web), Copyright Meta Platforms,
Inc., Apache License, Version 2.0. No toolkit code is included.

